 # Octree-based Level of Detail and Culling
 
-Also called: CPU Culling, LoD, CPU Frustum Culling, CPU-based Octree LOD & Frustum Culling, Distance-based LOD
+Also called: CPU Culling, LoD, CPU Frustum Culling, CPU-based Octree LOD & Frustum Culling, Distance-based LoD
 
 ## Overview
-This method reduces the rendering load of large point clouds by traversing a pre-built octree on the CPU to perform frustum culling and view-dependent sampling before uploading data to the GPU [S1]. It sets itself apart from GPU-based culling techniques by aggregating point data into cached averages at internal octree nodes, allowing the CPU to decide exactly which subset of points to render based on distance thresholds [S1].
+This method reduces the rendering load of large point clouds by traversing a pre-built octree on the CPU to perform frustum culling and view-dependent sampling before uploading data to the GPU [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from GPU-based culling techniques by aggregating point data into cached averages at internal octree nodes, allowing the CPU to decide exactly which subset of points to render based on distance thresholds [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 
 ### Inputs and Outputs
-*   **Input:** An octree structure built from a point cloud, where each node contains a bounding volume and a cached average point representing all points in its subtree [S1]. The current Model-View-Projection (MVP) matrix and camera eye position [S1].
-*   **Output:** A list of aggregated points (positions and colors) suitable for upload to a Vertex Buffer Object (VBO) for rendering as `GL_POINTS` [S1].
